WEBVTT

00:00:00.349 --> 00:00:03.605
Welcome to Stamp Page Designer, version eight.

00:00:03.655 --> 00:00:07.557
It's a free tool for making your own stamp album pages.

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:16.682
You place every stamp, title and story box yourself, and every stamp frame prints at its true size, so your stamps fit exactly.

00:00:17.983 --> 00:00:21.147
To start a new album, choose the margins first.

00:00:21.197 --> 00:00:27.987
Classic margins are one inch at the sides, and about one and a quarter inches at the top and bottom.

00:00:28.037 --> 00:00:32.638
Dense margins are half an inch all round, which gives you more room.

00:00:32.688 --> 00:00:37.015
If your pages go into a ring binder, tick the punch-hole margin.

00:00:38.316 --> 00:00:39.830
Next, pick the paper.

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:47.871
There is Letter, A4, Legal and A3, and twelve album page formats, such as Scott, Minkus and Stanley Gibbons.

00:00:47.921 --> 00:00:53.306
Then choose the spacing between items, across the page and down the page.

00:00:53.356 --> 00:00:58.294
The line under the paper shows exactly how big your usable area is.

00:00:59.616 --> 00:01:03.502
New in version eight, choose a look for the whole album.

00:01:03.552 --> 00:01:07.298
Standard, Classic, Contemporary, Modern or Minimalist.

00:01:07.348 --> 00:01:13.132
A look sets the lettering, the title, the page border and the lines, on every page.

00:01:13.182 --> 00:01:14.819
You can change it later.

00:01:16.149 --> 00:01:17.928
Then choose the first page.

00:01:17.978 --> 00:01:20.909
Leave it blank, or pick a ready-made layout.

00:01:20.959 --> 00:01:24.228
Give the album a name, and press Start designing.

00:01:25.549 --> 00:01:26.889
This is the editor.

00:01:26.939 --> 00:01:36.250
The navy bar at the top has Home, your album's name, Undo and Redo, Help, the keyboard shortcuts, and the size of the lettering.

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:40.639
On the right are just two buttons: Save album, and Save PDF.

00:01:41.949 --> 00:01:45.154
Below it is the Add bar, with eight buttons.

00:01:45.204 --> 00:01:49.445
Stamp, Title, Text, Picture, Frame, Line, Margin and Page.

00:01:49.495 --> 00:01:52.921
A button with a small arrow opens a short list.

00:01:52.971 --> 00:01:57.951
The Stamp list has every size, and the last size you used is marked.

00:01:58.001 --> 00:02:01.724
Picture, Frame, Line and Margin work straight away.

00:02:03.049 --> 00:02:04.877
Your pages are on the left.

00:02:04.927 --> 00:02:07.172
The page itself is in the middle.

00:02:07.222 --> 00:02:12.387
And the panel on the right shows the settings for whatever you've selected.

00:02:12.437 --> 00:02:17.810
Next to Settings is a new FAQ tab, with short answers to the common questions.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:22.886
At the foot of the pages, a small line tells you your work is being kept.

00:02:24.216 --> 00:02:26.950
Open the Title list, and add a Title.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:28.078
Type your text.

00:02:28.128 --> 00:02:29.357
Then pick a font.

00:02:29.407 --> 00:02:34.096
There are eighteen, and each one is shown in its own lettering.

00:02:34.146 --> 00:02:37.557
Then set the size, and make it bold or italic.

00:02:38.883 --> 00:02:43.203
Choose a height for the title box, from two to four centimetres.

00:02:43.253 --> 00:02:47.299
Fit the width to the text, and give it a border if you like.

00:02:47.349 --> 00:02:53.649
Once the box is narrower than the page, place it far left, left, centre, right, or far right.

00:02:54.983 --> 00:02:56.035
Now the stamps.

00:02:56.085 --> 00:03:00.295
The Stamp list holds Small, Medium, Large and Extra Large.

00:03:00.345 --> 00:03:06.245
Each adds a stamp frame of exactly that size, in the first free spot on the page.

00:03:06.295 --> 00:03:11.534
The button remembers the last size you used, so the next one is quicker.

00:03:12.849 --> 00:03:17.031
When you select a stamp, a small toolbar appears right above it.

00:03:17.081 --> 00:03:21.263
Change its size, add a caption, copy it, frame it, or delete it.

00:03:21.313 --> 00:03:26.023
And new in version eight, you can type the caption straight on the page.

00:03:26.073 --> 00:03:30.585
Press Caption, or double-click the stamp, then type, and press Enter.

00:03:31.916 --> 00:03:35.730
The panel on the right shows the size and caption first.

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:37.869
The rest is under More options.

00:03:37.919 --> 00:03:42.906
There you can type a short note inside the frame, like the stamp's value.

00:03:42.956 --> 00:03:49.599
And the frame line can be dashed, solid, or perforated, with little teeth like a real stamp edge.

00:03:50.916 --> 00:03:53.769
Every stamp can be resized with the mouse.

00:03:53.819 --> 00:03:56.810
Select it, and drag one of its blue corners.

00:03:56.860 --> 00:04:03.444
It grows in steps of one and a quarter millimetres, and it never goes past the edge of the page.

00:04:03.494 --> 00:04:05.517
If you go too far, press Undo.

00:04:06.849 --> 00:04:11.600
The Story box, in the Text list, is for your story about a stamp.

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:14.112
Type your text, and choose a size.

00:04:14.162 --> 00:04:21.424
New in version eight, a story box can have a pale fill behind it: grey, cream, blue, green or rose.

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:28.266
Picture opens a chooser first, so nothing lands on the page until you pick something.

00:04:28.316 --> 00:04:36.452
There are twenty-three line drawings, twenty classic stamp drawings, and two hundred and fifty-five flags, with a search box.

00:04:36.502 --> 00:04:39.923
You can also use your own picture from your computer.

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:43.447
To move anything, just drag it.

00:04:43.497 --> 00:04:48.520
When it comes near another item, its edges and centres pull into line.

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:52.507
Pink lines show you why, and blue numbers show the gap.

00:04:52.557 --> 00:04:55.769
To drag freely, hold Alt, or Option on a Mac.

00:04:57.083 --> 00:05:01.912
Copy and Paste put a copy right next to the original, one spacing away.

00:05:01.962 --> 00:05:04.455
You can even paste onto another page.

00:05:04.505 --> 00:05:11.809
Copy keeps the caption and the size, so it's the quickest way to add a row of stamps that are all the same.

00:05:13.116 --> 00:05:19.691
If items get too close, or overlap, they turn red, and a line above the page tells you about it.

00:05:19.741 --> 00:05:23.348
New in version eight, every warning comes with a fix.

00:05:23.398 --> 00:05:25.832
Show me selects the items concerned.

00:05:27.149 --> 00:05:31.950
And Fix: Auto-align this page, or the Auto-align button, puts it right.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:36.048
It evens out the spaces, and puts every edge on a grid line.

00:05:36.098 --> 00:05:41.513
Pictures and text stay where you put them, and Auto-align never shrinks a stamp.

00:05:42.816 --> 00:05:45.081
Frames go round a set of stamps.

00:05:45.131 --> 00:05:48.842
Select a few stamps, and press Frame on the toolbar.

00:05:48.892 --> 00:05:50.722
The frame fits round them.

00:05:50.772 --> 00:05:56.942
Choose one, two or three lines, or a stamp edge with perforation teeth, in any colour.

00:05:56.992 --> 00:05:59.329
A frame can have a pale fill too.

00:05:59.379 --> 00:06:02.150
Everything inside moves with the frame.

00:06:03.483 --> 00:06:11.729
The Title tab, in the Title list, sits on the corner of the page border, just like the country tab on printed album pages.

00:06:11.779 --> 00:06:16.352
Type the country, and add a flag before the text, after it, or both.

00:06:17.683 --> 00:06:20.305
A look styles the whole album at once.

00:06:20.355 --> 00:06:23.048
Under Page settings, choose Album look.

00:06:23.098 --> 00:06:24.384
The app asks first.

00:06:24.434 --> 00:06:31.416
Press Change the look, and the lettering, the titles, the border and the lines change on every page.

00:06:32.716 --> 00:06:35.181
Add page opens the layout gallery.

00:06:35.231 --> 00:06:37.178
Blank page is always first.

00:06:37.228 --> 00:06:43.170
Then there are nineteen layouts, in three groups: grids, rows, and special pages.

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:47.682
Each one is drawn for your album's paper, margins and border.

00:06:48.983 --> 00:06:53.098
Choose the stamp size at the top, and every picture redraws.

00:06:53.148 --> 00:06:57.263
If a layout needs a little less room, it says so underneath.

00:06:57.313 --> 00:07:01.220
And a layout that doesn't fit at that size is greyed out.

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:02.816
Nothing is ever shrunk.

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:06.511
New in version eight: My mounts add.

00:07:06.561 --> 00:07:13.074
If you use clear mounts, choose how much they add round each stamp, from one to three millimetres.

00:07:13.124 --> 00:07:15.552
You keep typing the stamp's own size.

00:07:15.602 --> 00:07:19.303
The printed border moves out to make room for the mount.

00:07:20.616 --> 00:07:23.891
Now press Import stamp list, and choose your file.

00:07:23.941 --> 00:07:29.077
The app asks where the stamps should go: into this album, or into a new album.

00:07:29.127 --> 00:07:33.665
The app puts up to eight stamps on a page, and never shrinks a stamp.

00:07:33.715 --> 00:07:38.719
Before any import, the app keeps a restore point, so you can always go back.

00:07:40.050 --> 00:07:43.500
As an album grows, finding one stamp gets harder.

00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:46.144
So there's a Find box above the page.

00:07:46.194 --> 00:07:50.574
Type part of a catalogue number or a caption, and press Enter.

00:07:50.624 --> 00:07:53.860
If several stamps match, you get a short list.

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:58.647
Click one, and the app goes to its page, and makes the stamp flash.

00:07:59.949 --> 00:08:02.923
Your work is kept automatically as you go.

00:08:02.973 --> 00:08:06.019
To keep an album for good, open Save album.

00:08:06.069 --> 00:08:09.690
Keep in this browser puts it in one of three slots.

00:08:11.016 --> 00:08:18.535
Save to my computer saves the whole album as one file, with your pictures inside, so you always have a copy.

00:08:18.585 --> 00:08:21.969
You can email it, or open it on another computer.

00:08:23.283 --> 00:08:25.811
When you're ready, press Save PDF.

00:08:25.861 --> 00:08:30.968
A small window asks which pages: all of them, this page, or a range.

00:08:31.018 --> 00:08:36.126
It shows a preview, and reminds you to print at one hundred percent.

00:08:36.176 --> 00:08:37.566
Press Make the PDF.

00:08:38.883 --> 00:08:41.805
That's Stamp Page Designer, version eight.

00:08:41.855 --> 00:08:46.262
It's free, it's open source, and it runs right in your browser.

00:08:46.312 --> 00:08:47.465
Happy collecting!
